      "content": "If your lawn is phosphorus deficient, you might notice that new growth appears stunted or pale, even if it's not fully yellow like a nitrogen issue. Older leaves might exhibit a dark green color, but the new shoots struggle to develop strongly. This deficiency usually shows up as general slow growth rather than widespread bleaching.",
