      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you notice clear signs of stunted, weak new growth, looking for a fertilizer with a higher middle number on the NPK ratio (the 'P') is a good strategy. However, because lawn health is complex, a balanced, slow-release fertilizer often works best initially. If the problem persists, consulting a local Portland nursery can help diagnose whether the issue is truly nutrient-related or something else, like compaction.",
